[{"client_msg_id":"26607ad0-7d9e-461e-b075-aa1cc6246e04","type":"message","user":"U9S4G0LJW","text":"めっちゃ便利だ","ts":"1634098132.038000","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"8HtY"}]},{"client_msg_id":"33c08761-d3ca-4af2-92e7-83f60ca91952","type":"message","user":"US5UW1UNB","text":"昨日の件でnvim lsp はキャンセルをすることができるみたいとわかったので、キャンセルを伝播させてそれを呼び出すこともできる。nvim lsp 使ってて、キャンセルしたい(たくさんタイプすると重くなるとか)というのがでてきたら使ってもいいかもね。僕は入れたことすらないのでそのへんのリアルな使用感はわかってない。","ts":"1634097203.037200","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"8Ua"}]},{"client_msg_id":"fab48b8c-374f-45c7-a180-54d11b794648","type":"message","user":"US5UW1UNB","text":"ddc-vim-lsp の差分を見てもらうとわかるかも。コード量半分ぐらいになっている\nvim側の関数呼び出しを await して待てる\nあとはリフレッシュによって後から追加、というのがなくなるのでソースやLS(重いやつ)によってはチラツキがなくなる\nリフレッシュは他のソースの再計算が走るのでそれがなくなる。\nそれらが合わさって高速化し、よりバグりにくくなる\nあとはキャンセルを検知できる","ts":"1634096853.034800","thread_ts":"1634058701.033800","subtype":"thread_broadcast","reactions":[{"name":"hee","count":3,"users":["U01BY3SDBRS","U9S4G0LJW","U72TB62UF"]},{"name":"sugoi","count":1,"users":["U76GA7MFA"]}],"replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"0wX"}],"root":{"client_msg_id":"b7cddc76-c8b2-41fb-9a71-0638605972c6","type":"message","user":"U9S4G0LJW","text":"実の所callbackで何が変わるのかいまいち分かってないマン","ts":"1634058701.033800","thread_ts":"1634058701.033800","reply_count":2,"team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"dtO"}]}},{"client_msg_id":"5e4909a8-961c-4d0b-8ccf-91d49b7e0318","type":"message","user":"U7TMPGWJ0","text":"`nvim-lspconfig` に設定が追加されたようなので存在を知りました \u003chttps://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig/commit/e4bed57f127310764f08e8b45f1ed3a31c6094e0\u003e","ts":"1634093794.034700","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"D/47"}]},{"c